    "chapter_name": "Probability",
    "year": "2014",
    "shift": "unknown_shift"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are two events such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the incorrect statement amongst the following statements is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are equally likely",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Using the addition theorem of probability,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0202_5cf8c72ae79f.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 182px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#39;</mi></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#39;</mi></msup><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are equally likely.</p><p>But we can&#39;t say that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>"
  }
}